{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ptr12gRH3EjxvDJumsdqKq","type":"tool_result","content":"10:2. The Job receives `TASK_CONTENT`, `TASK_ID`, `BRANCH`, `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, `MODEL`, etc. via env vars.\n19:| `TASK_CONTENT` | yes | — | Raw task markdown |\n35:1. Create a task file in OpenClaw vault with `assignee: claude-agent` (or a new assignee routed to this image via a Config CRD).\n37:3. Set `ALLOWED_TOOLS` on the Config CRD to the minimum tools the agent needs.\n40:### Config CRD env pattern\n42:The `Config` CRD's `spec.env` map becomes pod env vars, which `main.go` consumes via struct tags. Example from `k8s/github-update-go-agent.yaml`:\n46:  env:\n61:### Claude subprocess env allowlist\n63:`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be threaded explicitly via `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env map[string]string` in `main.go`. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default. See `docs/` for precedent (trade-analysis commit `1ccfa674cf`).\n88:- Unset session `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`\n90:  (`unset ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL ANTHROPIC_MODEL ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`). All\n91:  three are CLI flags with an env-var fallback (`main.go`,\n=== golangci\nversion: \"2\"\n\nrun:\n  timeout: 5m\n  tests: true\n\nlinters:\n  enable:\n    # Core\n    - govet\n    - errcheck\n    - staticcheck\n    - unused\n    - revive\n    - gosec\n    - gocyclo\n    - depguard\n    - dupl\n\n    # SRP & maintainability\n    - funlen\n    - gocognit\n    - nestif\n    - maintidx\n\n    # Readability & style\n    - errname\n    - unparam\n\n    # Safety / defensive coding\n    - bodyclose\n    - forcetypeassert\n    - asasalint\n    - prealloc\n  settings:\n    depguard:\n      rules:\n        Main:\n          deny:\n            - pkg: \"sigs.k8s.io/structured-merge-diff/v4\"\n              desc: \"use sigs.k8s.io/structured-merge-diff/v6 instead\"\n            - pkg: \"github.com/pkg/errors\"\n              desc: \"use github.com/bborbe/errors instead\"\n            - pkg: \"github.com/bborbe/argument\"\n              desc: \"use github.com/bborbe/argument/v2 instead\"\n            - pkg: \"golang.org/x/net/context\"\n              desc: \"use context from standard library instead\"\n            - pkg: \"golang.org/x/lint/golint\"\n              desc: \"deprecated, use revive or staticcheck instead\"\n            - pkg: \"io/ioutil\"\n              desc: \"deprecated since Go 1.16, use io and os packages instead\"\n\n    funlen:\n      lines: 80\n      statements: 50\n\n    gocognit:\n      min-complexity: 20\n\n    nestif:\n      min-complexity: 4\n\n    maintidx:\n      min-maintainability-index: 20\n\n    revive:\n      rules:\n        # Total-line limit matches the CLAUDE.md rule (file > 2000 lines = smell).\n        # skipBlankLines and skipComments are explicitly false so the count matches\n        # what `wc -l` reports and what readers see in editor scrollbars.\n        - name: file-length-limit\n          arguments:\n            - max: 2000\n              skipBlankLines: false\n              skipComments: false\n  exclusions:\n    presets:\n      - comments\n      - std-error-handling\n      - common-false-positives\n    rules:\n      - linters:\n          - staticcheck\n        text: \"SA1019\"\n      - linters:\n          - revive\n        path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"\n        text: \"dot-imports\"\n      - linters:\n          - revive\n        text: \"unused-parameter\"\n      - linters:\n          - revive\n        text: \"exported\"\n      - linters:\n          - dupl\n        path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"\n      - linters:\n          - errcheck\n        path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"\n      - linters:\n          - unparam\n        path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"\n      - linters:\n          - gosec\n        path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"\n\nformatters:\n  enable:\n    - gofmt\n    - goimports","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_f957bd7b98874acf90e3a141","session_id":"698f096f-a0f8-4a78-ad91-b84cbf89d0ae","uuid":"e77cb03e-5a98-41a7-923f-b60221d04712","timestamp":"2026-08-14T23:26:08.822Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec"}
